BMI Calculator

OIBSIP Task 2

A simple Python command-line BMI Calculator developed as part of the Oasis Infobyte internship.

Features

- Takes weight in kilograms as input.

- Takes height in meters as input.

- Calculates BMI using the formula:
  
  BMI = weight / (height²)

- Classifies BMI into:
  
  - Underweight
  - Normal
  - Overweight
  - Obese

- Displays the BMI rounded to 2 decimal places.

- Validates invalid and negative inputs.

- Displays helpful error messages.

Technologies Used

- Python
- input()
- Basic arithmetic
- Conditional statements
- Exception handling

How to Run

1. Make sure Python is installed.
2. Open the project folder in VS Code.
3. Open "bmi_calculator.py".
4. Run the program.
5. Enter your weight in kilograms.
6. Enter your height in meters.
7. The program displays your BMI and category.

BMI Categories

BMI Range| Category
Below 18.5| Underweight
18.5 – 24.9| Normal
25 – 29.9| Overweight
30 or above| Obese

